								<div class="title" id="post-title-4840155">
																	<a href="/forum/t-13863739/seeking-greenlight-keep-him-in-the-dark#post-4840155">Re: (Seeking Greenlight) Keep Him In The Dark</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607480670" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;" >Grigori Karpin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607480463 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Dec 2020 02:21</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13863739/seeking-greenlight-keep-him-in-the-dark">(Seeking Greenlight) Keep Him In The Dark</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840155">
									

<p>Called by PM</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So my concern here is that you’ve written yourself into a corner. SCP travels between dimensions, but doesn’t know. He can’t know. And in all of those dimensions he’s contained by the foundation.</p>
<p>The first thing I’d say is if the multiple foundation variants are aware that he’s going from containment cell to containment cell and not really aware of it, they could just leave well enough alone. Why try to stop his shifting? As long as the containment protocols are in place, he wouldn’t be able to breach in a traditional sense at all.</p>
<p>Second thing, because he’s just flitting from one containment cell to the next, this isn’t the most exciting of ideas. You can’t do wild stories because his life is prettt much always the same. AND because he doesn’t know, you also can’t develop his feelings about the matter because part of the premise is he’s ignorant.</p>
<p>Finally, it sorta beggars belief that all seven foundations have information sharing to the point where they have parallel files on him that are updated accordingly.</p>
<p>All in all, this seems like a much dryer version of the Unwilling Dimension Hopper skip from early on&#8230;</p>
<p>Without a completely rewritten concept at its core, I don’t know that this article would survive as you propose it currently.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

