<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An Euclid SCP (scp-xxx) that consists of an indestructible object (crown/trophy/statuette, i haven't decided yet) that has the ability teleport between any of two persons (hosts), upon the receiving host performing a specific ritual. Scp-xxx will also, trough unknown methods, transfer a seemingly random amount of money from the sender host to the receiver.</p>
<ul>
<li>list item</li>
</ul>
<p>Scp-xxx's ritual description can be relatively easily found in the internet, usually in the form of ads, like: &quot;MAKE A LOT OF MONEY WITH ONE WEIRD METHOD&quot;. It is unknown if these ads are generated by scp-xxx or another party.</p>
<ul>
<li>list item</li>
</ul>
<p>The ritual will change after the hosts rotate.</p>
<ul>
<li>list item</li>
</ul>
<p>People with low income tend to have more brand losses as sender hosts, but this is not reliable enough to make predictions</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The article will consist of research logs of the foundation trying to determine what dictates the amount of money that is transferred. The foundation will treat these research with a distinct urgency, that's because scp-xxx will withdraw copious amounts of money from the foundation while in its custody, between 5 - 50 million (i'm open to sugestions regarding this) generally a week after its containment.</p>
<p>Taking in account the worrying financial damage the foundation is undertaking while trying to contain scp-xxx, a deadline to cease scp-xxx containment has been set to avoid the foundation going bankrupt.</p>
<p>One foundation researcher was able to produce 100$, unfortunately the researched died in an unrelated accident. Since then, more hosts are being used to determine what caused this drop in transferred money .</p>
<p>Eventually the foundation found a D-class personnel refugy from [REDACTED] that produced a similar amount of money.</p>
<p>The rest will be available at the final draft.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
This should be an interesting scp since it poses more of a practical instead of being outright harmful to people.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
English is not my main language, so i might need extra help in grammar stuff</p>

